  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2022-02-18T06:13:50.940Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Cameras make for a hardcoded assumption of where the player's head is when you're over-rendering the player's viewpoint (eg; Stencil-based portals, or a HUD), but when you toggle from Standing to Seated mode while in VR that goes undetected and the viewpoint just sinks down into the floor because the camera thinks you're now crouching with all variables unchanged.  It'd be useful to have a bool or int variable to track the player's current VR state\nEg;\n0 = Seated\n1 = Standing\n2 = Full-Body Tracking",
